      "hp-science-statement": {
        "type": "hp-science-statement",
        "settings": {
          "heading_line_1": "The industry has been treating the symptom,",
          "heading_accent": "never the real problem.",
          "eyebrow": "WHY THE CATEGORY KEEPS FAILING",
          "paragraph_1": "A spot treatment clears the breakout before the barrier rebuilds. A hydration serum deposits moisture without activating the skin's own production. A brightening product suppresses melanin without addressing why it's being overproduced. Each product solves for the visible sign. None of them address the underlying biology that produced it.",
          "paragraph_2": "The result is a maintenance loop. The products work while you use them. The moment you stop, the original condition returns. Not because your skin is broken. Because nothing was ever rebuilt.",
